//! A doubly linked list implemented with `unsafe` Rust.
//!
//! # Safety invariants
//!
//! - Every node is owned by exactly one `Box<Node<T>>`: by `LinkedList::head`
//!   for the first node, and by the `next` field of the preceding node for all
//!   other nodes. `Node::prev` and `LinkedList::tail` are *non-owning* raw
//!   pointers.
//! - `LinkedList::head`, `LinkedList::tail` and every `Node::prev` point
//!   either to null or to a node owned by the list.
//! - While a `Cursor` is alive it holds the unique `&mut` to the list, so it
//!   is the only code that can reach the nodes. Its `current` pointer is
//!   always null or points to a node owned by the list.
//! - `LinkedList::len` always equals the number of nodes in the list.
//!
//! Raw pointers are stored as `*mut u8` instead of `*mut Node<T>` so that the
//! public types stay covariant in `T` (a raw `*mut Node<T>` field would make
//! them invariant).

// this module adds some functionality based on the required implementations
// here like: `LinkedList::pop_back` or `Clone for LinkedList<T>`
// You are free to use anything in it, but it's mainly for the test framework.
